      <node id="114146478736009652" label="114146478736009652">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '114146478736009652', 'user_id': '110556306817546253', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;DoomsdaysCW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; and people wonder why I am anti-nuclear...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Does safety mean nothing to profit-hungry people?  She sounds like a certain orange &quot;man&quot; in office who called himself a king.....&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-03-11 23:50:39', 'in_reply_to_id': '113653977309400523', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940019049850593" label="112940019049850593">
        <viz:color r="0" g="128" b="128" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940019049850593', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/Biden&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Biden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;’s $1.5 Billion Deal To Resurrect A &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/NuclearPlant&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;NuclearPlant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Is Facing Fresh Drama&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Story by Alexander C. Kaufman &lt;br&gt;August 9, 2024&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The United States’ effort to reverse the permanent shutdown of a nuclear station for the first time hit a potential snag this week when an ex-employee at the facility went public with safety concerns about reopening the 53-year-old power plant. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Now the company that owns the Palisades Nuclear Generating Station on Michigan’s southwest coast is hitting back at what it called a series of “assumptions” and “inaccurate statements” from Alan Blind, a former engineering director. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;Blind’s seven-year tenure overlapped with “a period when the plant performed poorly and required significant improvements” and ended nearly a decade before its closure two years ago, according to Florida-based &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/Holtec&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Holtec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; International, which bought the station from utility giant &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/Entergy&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Entergy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; following its shutdown in May 2022. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;In an unusually pointed 1,000-word rebuttal, Holtec said “significant investments, upgrades, and modifications were made by the prior owner to dramatically and measurably improve plant reliability” in the nine years after Blind’s departure. The company said the process is “on schedule” and announced at a public meeting this month that the plant is on track to reopen in October 2025.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;But Blind cast doubt on Holtec’s proposed budget and timeline for restoring &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/Palisades&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Palisades&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; given that no U.S. reactor has ever come back online after ceasing operations ahead of a planned demolition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;[...]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The money is going out. In January, the Biden administration put up $1.1 billion to keep California’s last nuclear power station [&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/DiabloCanyon&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;DiabloCanyon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;] from closing. Two months later, the Department of Energy offered Holtec a loan worth $1.5 billion to make Palisades the first U.S. nuclear plant to ever come back online after shutting down in preparation for decommissioning. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;At least two other utilities are now considering restarting shuttered nuclear reactors, including the unit at the &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/ThreeMileIsland&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;ThreeMileIsland&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; facility in Pennsylvania that did not melt down in 1979. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;On Monday, Reuters cited Blind saying the Palisades plant received waivers from the U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission that exempted the facility from modern safety standards that prevent insulation on pipes from breaking down and clogging cooling systems, guard against &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/earthquakes&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;earthquakes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and curb risks from &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/fires&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;fires&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Read more:&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/us/biden-s-15-billion-deal-to-resurrect-a-nuclear-plant-is-facing-fresh-drama/ar-AA1oxWha&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;msn.com/en-us/news/us/biden-s-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;15-billion-deal-to-resurrect-a-nuclear-plant-is-facing-fresh-drama/ar-AA1oxWha&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/RethinkNotRestart&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;RethinkNotRestart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/RenewablesNow&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;RenewablesNow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/NoNukes&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;NoNukes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/PalisadesNuclearPlant&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;PalisadesNuclearPlant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/NuclearPowerCorruptionAndLies&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;NuclearPowerCorruptionAndLies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/Michigan&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Michigan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/tags/WaterIsLife&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;WaterIsLife&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': ['palisades', 'palisades'], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 22:12:03', 'in_reply_to_id': None, 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940089015615294" label="112940089015615294">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940089015615294', 'user_id': '110684574673798400', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;DoomsdaysCW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br /&gt;Stupidity, one of the largest freshwater supplies in the US and the Government wants to FUCK IT UP.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 22:29:54', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940019049850593', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940185238119793" label="112940185238119793">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940185238119793', 'user_id': '110573668797904726', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;DoomsdaysCW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br /&gt;Story sounds similar to cars lots of us have owned. Sunk a bunch of cash into it and then sold it. Pretty rare that we made the moneypit awesome. Restorations are an exception but that&amp;#39;s a labour of love and craftsmanship, which is not what current business practices are about. The idea of beater with a heater nuclear plants seems a bit scary.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 22:54:23', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940019049850593', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940196741912268" label="112940196741912268">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940196741912268', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@kneworldodor&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;kneworldodor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Especially when nuclear embrittlement and concrete degradation can happen -- especially with older plants.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 22:57:17', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940185238119793', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940254013223144" label="112940254013223144">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940254013223144', 'user_id': '110573668797904726', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;DoomsdaysCW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; the only concrete I&amp;#39;ve heard of that ages gracefully is that self healing Roman stuff. I don&amp;#39;t think our modern buildings will stand the test of time as well. The way the world is it&amp;#39;s probably smart to consider how safe facilities will be if they are abandoned for any reason.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 23:11:52', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940196741912268', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940266956649768" label="112940266956649768">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940266956649768', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@kneworldodor&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;kneworldodor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Roman concrete is cool stuff. They cracked the recipe -- I think it involves volcanic ash and seawater? I think the Aztecs used something similar, but involving lava rock. There\'s so much we\'ve lost. And it was all done without plastic or PFAS or PCBs!&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 23:15:08', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940254013223144', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940676314376424" label="112940676314376424">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940676314376424', 'user_id': '110573668797904726', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;DoomsdaysCW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; not a 100% but I think the self healing comes from lime. The whole formula is the success story. We make so many stupid mistakes by cherry picking one or two ingredients from a solution and expecting the same results. We did this with addressing the drug problem locally and now the players are using the failure to say it doesn&amp;#39;t work. Copy the whole solution that others succeed with.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-11 00:59:16', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940266956649768', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940269527858659" label="112940269527858659">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940269527858659', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@kneworldodor&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;kneworldodor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Though there was asbestos involved sometimes. That wasn\'t good. Lead as well.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 23:15:48', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940254013223144', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940274416844691" label="112940274416844691">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940274416844691', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@kneworldodor&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;kneworldodor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Here\'s the thread. It was Mayan plaster. I also wrote about Roman concrete.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW/110238587434076527&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;kolektiva.social/@DoomsdaysCW/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;110238587434076527&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 23:17:03', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940254013223144', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940302318446179" label="112940302318446179">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '112940302318446179', 'user_id': '109367452842773908', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@kneworldodor&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;kneworldodor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; And on a personal note, my personal &quot;nemesis&quot; -- Seabrook Nuclear Power Plant -- is undergoing ASMR concrete degradation. For the same reason the Crane Estate in Ipswich started falling apart -- exposure to seawater, especially airborne seawater. Also, fun fact: they wanted to build the nuclear plant in Ipswich, MA, but the townspeople said, &quot;No.&quot; So then they went to Seabrook and the folks there were like, &quot;Jerbs!&quot; and said yes! I moved away soon after. I didn\'t want to live near the plant or the idiots that voted for it.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2024-08-10 23:24:08', 'in_reply_to_id': '112940254013223144', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="112940227482964477" label="112940227482964477">
