      <node id="113801396507310544" label="113801396507310544">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113801396507310544', 'user_id': '109304863828266555', 'content': '', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-10 01:11:42', 'in_reply_to_id': None, 'reblog': '113801392785125384'}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796353618275064" label="113796353618275064">
        <viz:color r="240" g="150" b="30" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796353618275064', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;This is a mind-numbing satellite image from Maxar Technologies of the wildfire in Altadena, posted at CNN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The hi-res composite image was taken at 10:45 a.m. PT by one of their LEO satellites and uses a mix of shortwave infrared and visible wavelengths. It shows nearly every building in western Altadena on fire 😢.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;JPL is just to the west of the NW quadrant of this image.&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cnn.com/weather/live-news/los-angeles-pacific-palisades-eaton-wildfires-01-08-25/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;cnn.com/weather/live-news/los-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;angeles-pacific-palisades-eaton-wildfires-01-08-25/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/tags/Wildfire&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Wildfire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/tags/Altadena&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Altadena&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/tags/JPL&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;JPL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;7/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': ['Altadena'], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 03:49:13', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796169052184062', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113793946474845492" label="113793946474845492">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113793946474845492', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;Wildfire map of LA area from NASA FIRMS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;NASA\'s Fire Information for Resource Management System (FIRMS) distributes Near Real-Time active fire data from the Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) aboard the Aqua and Terra satellites, and the Visible Infrared Imaging Radiometer Suite (VIIRS) aboard S-NPP, NOAA 20 and NOAA 21.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;JPL is closed except for emergency personnel. No fire damage so far but it is very close to the lab.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/map/#m:advanced;d:today;l:fires_landsat_landsat,fires_modis_aqua,fires_modis_terra,fires_viirs_noaa20,fires_viirs_noaa21,fires_viirs_snpp,countries,earth;@-118.08,33.96,10.53z&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;ap/#m:advanced;d:today;l:fires_landsat_landsat,fires_modis_aqua,fires_modis_terra,fires_viirs_noaa20,fires_viirs_noaa21,fires_viirs_snpp,countries,earth;@-118.08,33.96,10.53z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nasawatch.com/personnel-news/jpl-fire-update/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;nasawatch.com/personnel-news/j&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;pl-fire-update/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;1/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-08 17:37:03', 'in_reply_to_id': None, 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113794708140523045" label="113794708140523045">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113794708140523045', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;Some NASA services hosted at JPL are now offline or nonoperational.&lt;br&gt;E.g. - DSN now and JPL Horizons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The DSN Goldstone site in Barstow is probably OK.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The update from JPL at &lt;a href=&quot;https://nasawatch.com/personnel-news/jpl-fire-update/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;nasawatch.com/personnel-news/j&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;pl-fire-update/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; also stated that &quot;Hundreds of JPLers have been evacuated from their homes &amp;amp; many have lost homes. Special thx to our emergency crews. Pls keep us in your thoughts &amp;amp; stay safe.&quot;&lt;br&gt;🙏 &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pic below is from the Altadena area just east of JPL.&lt;br&gt;Credit: Josh Edelson/AFP via Getty Images&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/tags/Wildfire&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Wildfire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/tags/JPL&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;JPL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;2/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-08 20:50:45', 'in_reply_to_id': '113793946474845492', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113794746087566321" label="113794746087566321">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113794746087566321', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The JPL Emergency Page at &lt;a href=&quot;https://emergency.jpl.nasa.gov/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;emergency.jpl.nasa.gov/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has additional info -&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- JPL will remain closed until Monday, Jan 13&lt;br&gt;- All personnel are under mandatory telework with no Lab access except for designated personnel&lt;br&gt;- JPL facilities, labs and hardware are secured and protected.&lt;br&gt;- Deep Space Network (DSN) operations have been moved offsite to a back-up operations center.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-08 21:00:24', 'in_reply_to_id': '113794708140523045', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113795438630509191" label="113795438630509191">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113795438630509191', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The Wildland Fire Potential Index (WFPI) from the USGS forecasts the risk for large fire activity across the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is a unit-less number that ranges from 0 to 150 and relates to vegetation flammability. It describes the ratio of live to dead fuel and includes variables for wind speed, dry bulb temperature, and rainfall.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The wildfires in the L.A. area are not unexpected. The WFPI values around L.A. are mostly in the red zone. The Santa Ana winds spread the fire.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://firedanger.cr.usgs.gov/viewer/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;firedanger.cr.usgs.gov/viewer/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;4/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-08 23:56:32', 'in_reply_to_id': '113794746087566321', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796045018341280" label="113796045018341280">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796045018341280', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The wildfire situation around JPL looks very dire. This is a map of the wildfire in the area over the past 12 hours from the NASA FIRMS system. Note that there are a lot of residential areas underneath that red blob.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are certainly not prepared for natural disasters like this. We will be even less so after the new fossil-fueled, ravenous billionaire infused, sociopathic administration takes over.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/map/#m:advanced;d:2025-01-08%2014:10..2025-01-09%2002:10;l:fires_landsat_landsat,fires_modis_aqua,fires_modis_terra,fires_viirs_noaa20,fires_viirs_noaa21,fires_viirs_snpp,countries,earth;@-118.13,34.20,12.98z&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;ap/#m:advanced;d:2025-01-08%2014:10..2025-01-09%2002:10;l:fires_landsat_landsat,fires_modis_aqua,fires_modis_terra,fires_viirs_noaa20,fires_viirs_noaa21,fires_viirs_snpp,countries,earth;@-118.13,34.20,12.98z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;5/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 02:30:44', 'in_reply_to_id': '113795438630509191', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796169052184062" label="113796169052184062">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796169052184062', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;I hate posting videos of disasters. But I think people need to glimpse these to get a sense of the destruction and the human toll caused by these disasters, even though we may not have personally experienced them (yet). And the fact that these situations will only get worse unless we stop the billionaire class and the far-right from ravaging our dear earth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is CNN\'s Anderson Cooper reporting on the horrific scenes in the Altadena neighborhood east of JPL.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L45PLpkfvgM&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;youtube.com/watch?v=L45PLpkfvg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;M&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;6/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 03:02:17', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796045018341280', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796596867369716" label="113796596867369716">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796596867369716', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;This article from 2021 about prison inmates, incl teenagers, used as firefighters will make your blood boil.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;The inexpensive labor of incarcerated firefighters is a critical part of CA’s plan to get through wildfire season, which has become, as a symptom of the climate crisis, an almost year-round concern.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roughly 27% of the state’s firefighters were incarcerated in 2018 and 2019, earning mere dollars a day while free firefighters make an average $41.76 an hour.&quot;&lt;br&gt;😠&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.teenvogue.com/story/wildfire-camp-incarcerated-teens&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;teenvogue.com/story/wildfire-c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;amp-incarcerated-teens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;8/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:51:05', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796353618275064', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113798321804172596" label="113798321804172596">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113798321804172596', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;Here are devastating before-and-after satellite images from Maxar Technologies of a few blocks in Altaneda in visible light.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now let\'s imagine what it looks and feels like at street level.&lt;br&gt;Imagine households with young children, infants, the elderly, the disabled.&lt;br&gt;Houses full of memories. All gone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;These are horrific tragedies, made all the worse by Climate Change and an unholy union of billionaires and a political party that seem hell bent on making this worse.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2025-01-08/shocking-before-and-after-satellite-images-show-destruction-of-malibu-and-altadena-neighborhoods&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;latimes.com/california/story/2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;025-01-08/shocking-before-and-after-satellite-images-show-destruction-of-malibu-and-altadena-neighborhoods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;9/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 12:09:45', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796596867369716', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800300828879492" label="113800300828879492">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800300828879492', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The Eaton wildfire has reached the edge of the Mount Wilson Observatory area, north of Altadena 🙁 &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Power is out. The observatory website is down.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The site also hosts many towers for TV and radio transmission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Spo1lkghEY8&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;youtube.com/watch?v=Spo1lkghEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;10/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 20:33:03', 'in_reply_to_id': '113798321804172596', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800778223540945" label="113800778223540945">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800778223540945', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The map below shows the approx. location of the video camera at Mt. Wilson which is webcasting the video in the previous post. The camera is located high on a tower near the area with many TV towers. The smoke and small fires are located on the steep rightward slope.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Mount Wilson observatory is further east and at a higher elevation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.google.com/maps/place/Mt.+Wilson/@34.2263692,-118.0691144,429a,35y,100.8h,53.19t/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x80c2dd7871e3babb:0x94e3545e7f721aff!8m2!3d34.2264226!4d-118.0642319!16zL20vMDRfeXFo?entry=ttu&amp;amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDEwNy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;google.com/maps/place/Mt.+Wils&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;on/@34.2263692,-118.0691144,429a,35y,100.8h,53.19t/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x80c2dd7871e3babb:0x94e3545e7f721aff!8m2!3d34.2264226!4d-118.0642319!16zL20vMDRfeXFo?entry=ttu&amp;amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MDEwNy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;11/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 22:34:27', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800300828879492', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113806570458209926" label="113806570458209926">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113806570458209926', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The various aircraft supporting the fight against wildfires in CA include two &quot;Super Scooper&quot; Canadair CL-415 aircraft lent by Canada.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The CL-415 can scoop up to 6,140 L of water from a lake or ocean, optionally mix it with a chemical foam, and drop it on a fire without having to return to base to refill its tanks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The CL-415 needs a 12-second 410-metre-long run at 70 knots to scoop up the water and it requires considerable skill to fly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fuLk5hXMRZY&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;youtube.com/watch?v=fuLk5hXMRZ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;Y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadair_CL-415&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadair&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;_CL-415&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;12/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-10 23:07:30', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800778223540945', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113806624213422794" label="113806624213422794">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113806624213422794', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;Here is one of the &quot;Super Scooper&quot; Canadair CL-415 in action scooping up water off the coast near the Palisades.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;One of the two aircraft is grounded after it suffered some damage in a collision with a drone. Canada is sending more.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TLys5Wa7zhg&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;youtube.com/watch?v=TLys5Wa7zh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://skiesmag.com/news/canada-sending-more-aircraft-to-fight-california-wildfires/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;skiesmag.com/news/canada-sendi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;ng-more-aircraft-to-fight-california-wildfires/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;13/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-10 23:21:12', 'in_reply_to_id': '113806570458209926', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113811686537954268" label="113811686537954268">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113811686537954268', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;The Paliades wildfire is creeping north and east threatening communities like Brentwood, Encino, UCLA and West L.A.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Current wind conditions are allowing firefighters (from across CA, 7 other states, Canada and Mexico) to make progress in slowing down the advance of the wildfires.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But the National Weather Service is forecasting heightened fire weather conditions later today and into next week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/usfs/map/#d:2025-01-11;@-118.53,34.10,12.64z&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;sfs/map/#d:2025-01-11;@-118.53,34.10,12.64z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cnn.com/weather/live-news/los-angeles-wildfires-palisades-eaton-california-01-11-25/index.html&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;cnn.com/weather/live-news/los-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;angeles-wildfires-palisades-eaton-california-01-11-25/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;14/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-11 20:48:35', 'in_reply_to_id': '113806624213422794', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113811753865098659" label="113811753865098659">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113811753865098659', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;Map of evacuation zones around the Palisades wildfire. The mandatory evacuation zone now touches parts of I-405.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UCLA will hold classes online next week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gov. Newsom posted on X - &quot;We will be doubling the California National Guard on the ground to help fight the Los Angeles fires and keep our communities safe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We will now have 1,680 service members on the ground. We are grateful for their continued bravery and commitment to be of service to others.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.latimes.com/wildfires-map/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;&quot;&gt;latimes.com/wildfires-map/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;15/n&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-11 21:05:42', 'in_reply_to_id': '113811686537954268', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796440162362008" label="113796440162362008">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796440162362008', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; god&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;also&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;dat satellite tech&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:11:11', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796353618275064', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796469087144748" label="113796469087144748">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796469087144748', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; seriously can\'t get over the resolution of this IR data. you could see if someone\'s backyard BBQ was going&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:18:21', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796440162362008', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796525278347849" label="113796525278347849">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796525278347849', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;I suspect Maxar has even better resolution images than that for their paying customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Their newer satellites achieve 30-cm raw resolution. They also mention &quot;derived 15-cm high-definition (HD) imagery.&quot; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;You probably could apply your magic to bring out additional details.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.maxar.com/press-releases/maxar-intelligence-releases-first-images-from-its-next-generation-worldview-legion-satellites&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://www.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;maxar.com/press-releases/maxar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;-intelligence-releases-first-images-from-its-next-generation-worldview-legion-satellites&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:32:52', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796469087144748', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796599026142025" label="113796599026142025">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796599026142025', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Not sure what they mean by derived, but presumably 30 cm raw visible light resolution is a bit lower in the infrared, maybe more like 40-60cm, but still obvious enough to see if someone\'s BBQ is flaring up... I put the lower limit at flaming bag of poop, if it gets hot enough&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:51:38', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796525278347849', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796626546481313" label="113796626546481313">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796626546481313', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;Question - If you had multiple images of a scene, taken at different times at slightly different spatial offsets and angles (dithering), could they be processed to &quot;derive&quot; a higher effective resolution image?&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:58:38', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796599026142025', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796713189948572" label="113796713189948572">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796713189948572', 'user_id': '109258955291784011', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes. Astrophotographers regularly do sth similar called “drizzling”, especially for planetary photography which is usually done by taking raw video to get 1000s of shots, the best of which are selected and combined (“stacked”). Drizzling is one technique in there to increase effective resolution.&lt;br&gt;See &lt;a href=&quot;https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drizzle_(image_processing)&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drizzl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;e_(image_processing)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 05:20:42', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796626546481313', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796819132932895" label="113796819132932895">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796819132932895', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.online/@databu&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;databu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; I\'m not sure how that would work with something as dynamic as a scene on earth, though. Drizzling is the first thing that came to mind, but &quot;derived&quot; could mean anything these days.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 05:47:36', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796713189948572', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796884591352030" label="113796884591352030">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796884591352030', 'user_id': '109258955291784011', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; is it really that much more dynamic when compared to planetary images which are affected by seeing? I’m not an expert in the internals of drizzle algorithms, but they must be able to cope with quite some variance?&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 06:04:17', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796819132932895', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796954821566916" label="113796954821566916">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796954821566916', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.online/@databu&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;databu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for planetary images and all the seeing problems introduced by the atmosphere they are using something called &quot;lucky&quot; imaging. Taking a whole bunch of them (thousands) and then sifting through all of them for the best, least distorted ones to combine into a final image. I\'m not really sure that Wikipedia article is really correct.... but maybe I\'m the wrong one! I\'ve only messed with drizzling a handful of times. I always assumed it needed four virtually pristine images with a subpixel shift... not, say, something with people walking around, or perspective changes from a satellite orbiting. Then again the satellite may actually take exposures that quickly.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 06:22:06', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796884591352030', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113797418927905074" label="113797418927905074">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113797418927905074', 'user_id': '109258955291784011', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; as far as I know, lucky imaging is actually a simplified name for a multi-stage process: 1. A subset of best-quality images (there might not actually be any really pristine ones, depending on the conditions), and 2. Stacking algorithms which reject individual pixels from individual selected images based on statistical measurements. This might catch walking people etc.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 08:20:10', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796954821566916', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113797419856071799" label="113797419856071799">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113797419856071799', 'user_id': '109258955291784011', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; But I’m not sure how drizzle is implemented within that flow, so it might or might not apply in this case.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 08:20:24', 'in_reply_to_id': '113797418927905074', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113798627072643646" label="113798627072643646">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113798627072643646', 'user_id': '108307836330188350', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.online/@databu&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;databu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; It\'s definitely a machine learning method. Not sure how I feel about it being applied to analytical data...&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.maxar.com/earth-intelligence/2020/hd-satellite-imagery-and-machine-learning-more-accurately-detect-and-locate-features-of-interest-with-greater-consistency?utm_source=blog&amp;amp;utm_medium=organic&amp;amp;utm_campaign=51-cm-hd&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;blog.maxar.com/earth-intellige&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;nce/2020/hd-satellite-imagery-and-machine-learning-more-accurately-detect-and-locate-features-of-interest-with-greater-consistency?utm_source=blog&amp;amp;utm_medium=organic&amp;amp;utm_campaign=51-cm-hd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 13:27:25', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796819132932895', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796674433466484" label="113796674433466484">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796674433466484', 'user_id': '109268980483243765', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Or, you know, the tailpipe of a T-90 tank.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Commercial imagery is very much a side business for Maxar.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 05:10:50', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796469087144748', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796830397968739" label="113796830397968739">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796830397968739', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://social.linux.pizza/@simonbp&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;simonbp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; I was trying to avoid realistic topics. 😔&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 05:50:28', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796674433466484', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796864079116713" label="113796864079116713">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796864079116713', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://social.linux.pizza/@simonbp&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;simonbp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;Doesn\'t the NRO have higher resolution satellites, with higher number of wavelengths/bands as well as SAR?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Although the article below mentions NRO\'s contracts with Maxar and other imaging satellite companies.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://euro-sd.com/2024/07/articles/39425/the-black-world-of-us-spy-satellites/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;euro-sd.com/2024/07/articles/3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;9425/the-black-world-of-us-spy-satellites/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 05:59:03', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796674433466484', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796882817800068" label="113796882817800068">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796882817800068', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://social.linux.pizza/@simonbp&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;simonbp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; The NRO buys a lot of data (millions of dollars per year) from commercial satellites, including Maxar optical data and SAR from Capella, Umbra, and ICEYE. They like to get data that is unclassified and can easily be shared with allies, even if they have better classified images.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 06:03:50', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796864079116713', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113832990903726477" label="113832990903726477">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113832990903726477', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;Here is some additional zoomable hi-res imagery of the fire-affected areas in LA from the National Geodetic Survey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Can\'t tell which satellites and other assets they use to generate these maps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Actually they do mention MAXAR at the bottom right corner of the map.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://storms.ngs.noaa.gov/storms/2025_eri/index.html#17.61/34.188576/-118.131741&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;storms.ngs.noaa.gov/storms/202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;5_eri/index.html#17.61/34.188576/-118.131741&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 15:06:35', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796469087144748', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833151778000196" label="113833151778000196">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833151778000196', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, I have seen a Maxar very-high-resolution satellite image acquired on Jan. 10 in several viewers.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 15:47:31', 'in_reply_to_id': '113832990903726477', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833225172973570" label="113833225172973570">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833225172973570', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;  Thanks for the link to the NOAA viewer, it is much more informative with the streets labeled and other annotation. The Maxar images I saw before were hard to navigate. The data may be the same, but the NOAA viewer is much better.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:06:11', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833151778000196', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833289441175922" label="113833289441175922">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833289441175922', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;We can see how close to JPL the fires got. Most houses east of Lincoln Ave in the map look burned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://storms.ngs.noaa.gov/storms/2025_eri/index.html#15.41/34.198076/-118.163023&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;storms.ngs.noaa.gov/storms/202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;5_eri/index.html#15.41/34.198076/-118.163023&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:22:29', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833225172973570', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833303503783594" label="113833303503783594">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833303503783594', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, I believe the closest house that was completely destroyed was about 400 meters east of the East Gate of JPL (where the bridge crosses the Arroyo Seco river). The building where I work is another 400 meters further west.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:26:06', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833289441175922', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833308872626863" label="113833308872626863">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833308872626863', 'user_id': '111183118329973316', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 😱 ☹️&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:27:27', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833303503783594', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833309750094104" label="113833309750094104">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833309750094104', 'user_id': '109289083987093825', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That\'s the Arroyo Seco in between - as the name indicates, it is dry, and a good fire break.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:24:43', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833289441175922', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833351534717272" label="113833351534717272">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833351534717272', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@TMEubanks&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;TMEubanks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, the Arroyo Seco is a good firebreak for slowly moving ground fires, but I am not sure it would have stopped the streams of burning embers that were blowing in the wind, if the fire had reached the last line of houses across from JPL.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 16:38:19', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833309750094104', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833453797167368" label="113833453797167368">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833453797167368', 'user_id': '109289083987093825', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, but JPL is also a harder target - few trees, no significant wooden buildings, most flat fire-proof roofs, etc.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 17:04:14', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833351534717272', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833461923474115" label="113833461923474115">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833461923474115', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@TMEubanks&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;TMEubanks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;Glad you did not get to test these features against a real firestorm.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 17:06:22', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833453797167368', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833535445906863" label="113833535445906863">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833535445906863', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@TMEubanks&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;TMEubanks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, JPL has been hardened against fire in many ways, but we had previously expected the fire to approach from the north through the mountains. A previous fire, the 2009 Station Fire got within 300 meters of JPL northern edge, but there was no wind that day. The winds last week were unusually strong and damaged several buildings at JPL without the fire reaching the campus.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 17:25:05', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833461923474115', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833569549523797" label="113833569549523797">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833569549523797', 'user_id': '109246743437611105', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@TMEubanks&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;TMEubanks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; The area near the East Gate is the oldest part of JPL and includes Building 11 that was built around 1940, long before there were advanced fire-resistant building designs. I am sure it has been upgraded since it was built but I bet it has a wood frame inside.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 17:33:45', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833535445906863', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113833615668523250" label="113833615668523250">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113833615668523250', 'user_id': '109289083987093825', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@EricFielding&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;EricFielding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://astrodon.social/@spacegeck&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;spacegeck&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Yes, when I was at JPL that part of the Lab had older &quot;temporary&quot; buildings made of wood, but with metal roofs.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-15 17:45:28', 'in_reply_to_id': '113833569549523797', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796506230457060" label="113796506230457060">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796506230457060', 'user_id': '109333434738348730', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;  OMFG   💔&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:28:03', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796353618275064', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113796618382721046" label="113796618382721046">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113796618382721046', 'user_id': '109292615673959645', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; I couldn\'t even bear to look at the state voting results after I caught a glance at a headline or a post somewhere and realized we failed to end carceral slave labor, aka our prisoner firefighters. A lot of us thought that was going to be an easy win in a state like CA.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 04:56:33', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796596867369716', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113797558432811304" label="113797558432811304">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113797558432811304', 'user_id': '113441875009089907', 'content': '&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;California: We have this economically efficient plan to fight wildfires!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;*looks inside*&lt;br&gt;slavery', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 08:55:39', 'in_reply_to_id': '113796596867369716', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800338304515151" label="113800338304515151">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800338304515151', 'user_id': '108198050614861612', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mount Stromlo Observatory, 2003 fires.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 20:42:35', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800300828879492', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800525761782785" label="113800525761782785">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800525761782785', 'user_id': '1135273', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Right now Mt Wilson observatory is fine, fireline is half a km south, winds blowing towards fire, not towards observatory. It&amp;#39;s looking not bad.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 21:30:17', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800300828879492', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800553093502729" label="113800553093502729">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800553093502729', 'user_id': '1135273', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://social.sciences.re/@jaztrophysicist/113800425598241182&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;social.sciences.re/@jaztrophys&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;icist/113800425598241182&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 21:37:14', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800525761782785', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113800607948817101" label="113800607948817101">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113800607948817101', 'user_id': '109247255215674808', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/@knud&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;knud&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br&gt;The images from the live video on YouTube does show some vegetation on fire very close to those TV/radio/cell towers and buildings. The wind keeps shifting direction on that steep slope. Let\'s hope those fires die out.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-09 21:51:10', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800525761782785', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113803095764967189" label="113803095764967189">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113803095764967189', 'user_id': '1135273', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://social.sciences.re/@jaztrophysicist&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;jaztrophysicist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In the end it was a close call but the fire didn&amp;#39;t go further than in the video:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastodon.social/tags/MountWilsonObservatory&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;MountWilsonObservatory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-10 08:23:52', 'in_reply_to_id': '113800607948817101', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113807327318650097" label="113807327318650097">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113807327318650097', 'user_id': '109443599273035345', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Is the salt water not causing it problems?&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-11 02:20:00', 'in_reply_to_id': '113806624213422794', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="113806709894034670" label="113806709894034670">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '113806709894034670', 'user_id': '109417467433120893', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot; translate=&quot;no&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fosstodon.org/@AkaSci&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;AkaSci&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; I was at an airshow decades ago and one of the Canadian water tankers performed. Don\'t recall which model. Watching the pilot maneuver something that large in such a tight space was damn impressive. Stole the show. There were military flybys and even a military demonstration team at the event but what I recall all these years later is the skill of that pilot and the agility of that aircraft.&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2025-01-10 23:42:59', 'in_reply_to_id': '113806570458209926', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
