      <node id="110648062926285096" label="110648062926285096">
        <viz:color r="240" g="150" b="30" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '110648062926285096', 'user_id': '109321601315889133', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://m.ai6yr.org/tags/Missing&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Missing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://m.ai6yr.org/tags/Hiker&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Hiker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a href=&quot;https://m.ai6yr.org/tags/Altadena&quot; class=&quot;mention hashtag&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#&lt;span&gt;Altadena&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Missing hiker, Albert Zisook, a resident of Los Angeles County, was last seen on July 1, 2023, at 6:00 a.m., near Chaney Trail and Alta Loma Drive in Altadena.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mr. Zisook is 5’7”, 165 lbs., with gray hair and blue eyes.  He was last seen wearing glasses. &lt;a href=&quot;https://local.nixle.com/alert/10178985/?sub_id=0&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;https://&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ellipsis&quot;&gt;local.nixle.com/alert/10178985&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;invisible&quot;&gt;/?sub_id=0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': ['Altadena'], 'created_at': '2023-07-03 03:37:12', 'in_reply_to_id': None, 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="110648086728603550" label="110648086728603550">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '110648086728603550', 'user_id': '109321601315889133', 'content': &quot;&lt;p&gt;Hard to get lost over there as you can see the lights of LA most of the time. I'll put my money on either 1. medical emergency or 2. he's stuck down in this canyon, went down a trail he couldn't come back out on, near Millard Falls. I know the folks at the SAR group there, dunno who the search manager is since I am no longer involved in that stuff. They'll be running cell phone pings by now trying to localize him.&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2023-07-03 03:43:22', 'in_reply_to_id': '110648062926285096', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="110651316068277395" label="110651316068277395">
        <viz:color r="190" g="190" b="190" a="1.0" />
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="{'id': '110651316068277395', 'user_id': '109530100029206936', 'content': '&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;h-card&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://m.ai6yr.org/@ai6yr&quot; class=&quot;u-url mention&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@&lt;span&gt;ai6yr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; hard also to get lost as these trails are so well maintained. (if, of course, you stay on them.) i was thinking medical emergency too. i hope they find him safe. 🤞&lt;/p&gt;', 'tags': [], 'created_at': '2023-07-03 17:24:48', 'in_reply_to_id': '110648086728603550', 'reblog': None}" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
